 "description": "Bae2017 - Mathematical analysis of circadian disruption and metabolic re-entrainment of hepatic gluconeogenesis\nBioModels BIOMD0000001005 (curated). SBML file: Bae2018.xml.\nSimulation: 0 to 480 time units (SED-ML: Bae2018.sedml), sampling 5.\nRun switches: -ig:mass -INT:1 -obeymaxint\nVerification against libRoadRunner (SBML reference): PASS, max |difference| = 7.11e-04 of species peak (worst: y1)\nSBML time units are used unchanged as Kintecus seconds.\nConversion notes:\n  [info] ACTH_Degradation: rate is not proportional to its reactants; divided form used with 1/(c+1e-30) so an empty species is not consumed\n  [info] F_HPA__Degradation: rate is not proportional to its reactants; divided form used with 1/(c+1e-30) so an empty species is not consumed\n  [info] CRH_Degradation term 1/2: rate is not proportional to its reactants; divided form used with 1/(c+1e-30) so an empty species is not consumed\n  [info] CRH_Degradation term 2/2: rate is not proportional to its reactants; divided form used with 1/(c+1e-30) so an empty species is not consumed\n  [info] CRH_Degradation term 2/2: USER expression is 1901 characters; Kintecus V2027 mis-evaluates USER expressions longer than about 840 characters (see KINTECUS_ISSUES)\n  [info] NMN_to_NAD: rate is not proportional to its reactants; divided form used with 1/(c+1e-30) so an empty species is not consumed\n  [info] NAD_Inhibition: rate is not proportional to its reactants; divided form used with 1/(c+1e-30) so an empty species is not consumed\n  [info] NAD_to_NAM: rate is not proportional to its reactants; divided form used with 1/(c+1e-30) so an empty species is not consumed\n  [info] NAM_to_NMN: rate is not proportional to its reactants; divided form used with 1/(c+1e-30) so an empty species is not consumed\n  [info] SIRT1_Degradation: rate is not proportional to its reactants; divided form used with 1/(c+1e-30) so an empty species is not consumed\n  [info] PGC1aN_to_PGC1aNactive: rate order differs from the stoichiometry; consumed on separate line(s) - PGC1aN: zero order, signed\n  [info] MR_Degradation: rate is not proportional to its reactants; divided form used with 1/(c+1e-30) so an empty species is not consumed\n  [info] GR_Degradation: rate is not proportional to its reactants; divided form used with 1/(c+1e-30) so an empty species is not consumed\n  [info] P_cyt_mRNA_Production term 3/8: rate order differs from the stoichiometry; consumed on separate line(s) - mRNAP: zero order, signed\n  [info] P_cyt_mRNA_Production term 4/8: rate order differs from the stoichiometry; consumed on separate line(s) - mRNAP: zero order, signed\n  [info] P_cyt_mRNA_Production term 6/8: rate order differs from the stoichiometry; consumed on separate line(s) - mRNAP: zero order, signed\n  [info] P_cyt_mRNA_Production term 7/8: rate order differs from the stoichiometry; consumed on separate line(s) - mRNAP: zero order, signed\n  [info] P_cyt_Receptor_mRNA_Production term 2/2: rate order differs from the stoichiometry; consumed on separate line(s) - mRNARP: zero order, signed\n  [info] GR_Degradation_copy: rate is not proportional to its reactants; divided form used with 1/(c+1e-30) so an empty species is not consumed\n  [partial] CRH_Degradation term 2/2: Kintecus V2027 mis-reads this long USER expression (FATAL #999 or a wrong value) in every equivalent form tried\n  [partial] Feed_2 term 2/2: Kintecus V2027 mis-reads this long USER expression (FATAL #999 or a wrong value) in every equivalent form tried\nRenamed species (Kintecus name = SBML id): P1 = P",
